About YARFRAW

	<<Y>>et <<A>>nother <<R>>ss <<F>>eed <<R>>eader <<A>>nd <<W>>riter is an open source API library 
for working with RSS feed. It offers a set of data model in builder style to help developer build RSS 2.0 feed.
(Supports for  RSS 0.9x, RSS 1.0 / RDF, Atom 0.3 and Atom 1.0 will come in later releases).

Why Another Java RSS API?

	Sure there are many of such libraries, but in software (and anything eles) there are always room for 
	improvement. Someone else already did it is not a good reason for stopping new developments. The goal of this
	project is to provide an intuitive, high quality alternative to all these other similar libraries. 
	
	Another reason is that I think this push down publishing is just a wonderful idea. I wish every every website
would offer a rss feed (now most the popular ones already do). It allows users to process much more information than they
normally would (by visiting the website). Ever since I started using Google's Rss Reader, I can browse through the same
amount of information that would normally take me twice as much time to do. If you are thinking about adding a Rss feed
to your website, you really should.

Project Status

	The API is now at a stable stage and fully supports RSS 2.0 feeds, you can use it in your projects. I am 
currently lookup for developers/volunteers to share some of the workload of this project. If you are interested
in helping out, send me a message at 'zl25-drexel AT gmail DOT com'. (You need to be reasonably proficient with
Java, XML, Maven2, SVN and open source development in general). 
		